    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on exploiting favorable matchups against sub-5.00 xERA starters, led by our premier offensive anchor, **Kyle Tucker** (77.96). Facing McCullers Jr., **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a strong SP skill advantage that boosts his output to elite territory. He is joined by **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Gunnar Henderson** (73.50) as our high-ceiling core. **Jackson Merrill** is particularly intriguing; despite the minor negative modifier for a sub-2.00s pop-time catcher, his aggressive role at the top of the order against Houser creates a 75+ efficiency profile, while **Gunnar Henderson** remains a must-start not only for his 14% platoon boost against P\u00e9rez but for the added aggressive-baserunning equity generated by the opposing pitcher's slow delivery.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Nolan Schanuel** (55.01), who hovered just outside the starting threshold but ultimately fell short due to the high density of players like **Brady House** (61.59) and **Andy Pages** (65.43) holding higher efficiency scores against weaker opposing arms. **Miguel Vargas** (61.83) and **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) capitalize on the high xERA of Ure\u00f1a, with **Sam Antonacci**\u2019s elite xwOBA metrics making him an indispensable piece of today's tactical stack. While we remain confident in this configuration, **Jacob Wilson** (45.36) represents a marginal start today, hampered significantly by a -19% SP skill penalty when facing the dominant arm of Wheeler. We are proceeding with the current alignment, but managers should monitor weather patterns closely, as any shift could further dampen the appeal of our lower-scored starters like **Heliot Ramos** (44.75).",
